/*
 * Shared test fixture — not shipped in any package.
 *
 * Ground truth for data/ships/pre-engineered.jsonc — the module variants that arrive already
 * modified, whether bought from the Merc-Coin shop, awarded by an event or community goal, or
 * unlocked at a tech broker. A pre-engineered module has no symbol of its own, so each record pairs
 * a base module `symbol` (joins to the module catalogues) with the journal `blueprintSymbol` identity
 * baked in, the `grade` already applied, and an optional `experimentalEffectSymbol`. The three festive event
 * rewards carry grade-5 `Decorative_*` identities. `engineeringLocked` marks final articles that
 * accept no further engineering: the seven Guardian-weapon variants and the five fixed Enzyme/AX
 * variants. No narrower key than the (symbol, blueprintSymbol, grade, experimentalEffectSymbol)
 * tuple is unique across the catalogue — the medium Guardian Shard
 * Cannon carries Long Range with no experimental twice, at two different grades. `counts` pins the
 * catalogue size and its split by acquisition; `records` pins individual pairings;
 * `modifierCounts` and `modifierLabels` pin the hand-set stat blocks that make a variant fittable;
 * `burstIntervalVariants` pins the variants that change a burst pattern, so the modifier that
 * drives their rate of fire cannot be dropped again, each with the `rateOfFire` the resolved
 * article carries and the `blockRateOfFire` its published engineering block states — one
 * article states one rate of fire, so the two are the same figure; `mercenaryBakedEffects` pins
 * Merc-shop rows sold with an experimental effect already applied. Each shop row also carries
 * its fixed grade-1 transformation;
 * `resolved` pins whole stat blocks against known in-game values; `identification.mercenary`
 * pins the Mercenary-only blueprint identity
 * that survives later grade upgrades; `mercCoin` pins shop prices; `joins` pins that every
 * record resolves against the module, blueprint and experimental catalogues.
 */
